{"id": "EUVD-2026-81845", "enisaUuid": "fffd4969-a6ba-34f0-8503-c6810b832ee5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: MGMT: free the HCI command when it is cancelled\n\nmgmt_hci_cmd_sync() queues the pending command with a NULL destroy\ncallback, so it is only freed if send_hci_cmd_sync() runs. A cancelled\nentry is leaked, as _hci_cmd_sync_cancel_entry() does not release\nentry->data when there is no destroy callback, and hci_cmd_sync_clear()\ncancels every pending entry when the controller is unregistered. Nothing\nelse reclaims it either: mgmt_pending_new() does not put the command on\nhdev->mgmt_pending.\n\nThe leak also pins the socket reference taken by mgmt_pending_new(), so\nthe mgmt socket is never released.\n\nFree the command from a destroy callback. The now-empty done label is\nreplaced by a direct return.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:00:29", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0cd7b34dc6b5414cac3d4cd376f73d3e9ffbd93", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/481533b03985177ddc805e0bd12fc07e7adf9040", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/414b365ecea6c30357adee6b8a7c5edc03a03575"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90252", "GHSA-9q76-v4mr-q636"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14a6b00c-4a23-3146-9c51-09da1f358912", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "827af4787e74e8df9e8e0677a69fbb15e0856d2f <414b365ecea6c30357adee6b8a7c5edc03a03575"}, {"id": "320ff0c9-0e06-357b-9e6b-b010513f8a7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.13"}, {"id": "4e5d8cfc-3d8e-3a56-aa35-f807a1ba3950", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "827af4787e74e8df9e8e0677a69fbb15e0856d2f <e0cd7b34dc6b5414cac3d4cd376f73d3e9ffbd93"}, {"id": "6ba1eacd-8059-35b2-9602-e6a8d25b9967", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "954bae1b-9140-38be-b619-0072921b1d56", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e6233ee9-d3e1-3c6e-8354-1188d459e58d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "827af4787e74e8df9e8e0677a69fbb15e0856d2f <481533b03985177ddc805e0bd12fc07e7adf9040"}, {"id": "f1f8d2cd-778c-3d24-ad07-99c271f888a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "f3303b6e-dc28-3440-bb13-907d6e1dbf93", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "86ca2f78-be95-3bac-ac5e-2973879c82d2", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}